error[NK1284]: `Scanner.at` holds a `text::Pos`, and a position is no field: nothing ties it to the text it belongs to.
  --> tests/text_pos_is_no_field.nika:7:5
   |
 7 |     at: text::Pos,
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A position belongs to exactly one text, which the compiler follows through names, parameters and branches; a field keeps its own sources, so a text field beside it is no tie (ADR-374 D5, D6).
   = help: Hold the text and the position together in a `text::Cursor`: `text::Cursor(t)`, `c.at()`, `c.go(p)`, `c.until(needle)`, `c.rest()`.
error[NK1284]: `Marks.seen` holds a `text::Pos`, and a position is no field: nothing ties it to the text it belongs to.
   --> tests/text_pos_is_no_field.nika:11:5
    |
 11 |     seen: Vec[text::Pos?],
